  "notes": "Modified cash basis. Governmental from the governmental funds statement p4 Totals column. The statement's Taxes 247,142, Intergovernmental 182,395 and Other 51,603 lines are split by the printed rows of the fund budget schedules (General p10, Street p12, Economic Development p14), which add exactly to each line. Business-type from the proprietary statement p6-8 Totals (cash-only assets, so measure cash). Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position - Modified Cash Basis (2024 Totals); no liabilities. Detail: each governmental fund's own budget schedule (p10-16); the all-funds budgetary statement p9 is not recorded (no double counting); proprietary funds from the combined proprietary budget schedule p17. Community Development spending is the Economic Development Fund (operations and grants to businesses), recorded as economic development. Read pages 1-17 of 17"
